# walkthrough.out -- the portable discipline suite run end to end on this example project.
# Reproduce: cd example; cp -r ../discipline ../*.sh ../registers . && touch .discipline; then run the commands below in order.

== self-tests ==
-- python3 -m discipline.forced --self

  self-test: 0.5 declared as 1/2 does not row; 0.37 does.
   exit 0
-- python3 -m discipline.ground --self

  self-test: the self-contained file with a MIRRORS block does not row; the importing one rows twice.
   exit 0
-- python3 -m discipline.primitive --self

  self-test: two identical copies register and pass; changing one to x*2 rows as drift; an identical pair the register does not hold rows as unregistered.
   exit 0
-- python3 -m discipline.cited --self

  self-test: the imported citation does not row; the untouched one does.
   exit 0

== python3 example.py ==
  [SQ1] DECLARED  predicts: for every n from 1 to 200 the sum of the first n odd numbers is a perfect square
  [SQ1]           kills:    an n in 1..200 whose sum of the first n odd numbers is not a perfect square
  [SQ1]           control:  the sum of the first n even numbers is a perfect square, which must fail
  [SQ1]           budget:   formulation 1 of 3
  [SQ1] 0 violating rows (of the examined set; see the section's count line)
  SQ1 HOLDS.  200 of 200 sums are squares
  control even-ctrl: fails as it must.  200 of 200 even sums are not squares
  control even-ctrl: silent on 0 of 200 rows

  ============================== referee ==============================
       SQ1  HOLDS      predicted: for every n from 1 to 200 the sum of the first n odd numbers is a perfect square
  REFEREE: 1 of 1 declared claims hold; 1 control(s) failed as required.  The run counts.
   exit 0

== python3 broken.py ==
  [B1] DECLARED  predicts: something holds
  [B1]           kills:    it does not
  [B1]           budget:   formulation 1 of 3
  B1 REFUSED.  literal verdict.  this verdict was typed, not computed

  ============================== referee ==============================
        B1  NO VERDICT predicted: something holds
  REFEREE: the run does not count.  Reasons:
    - B1: verdict argument is a literal -- the verdict must be computed
    - no negative control ran
   exit 1

